@packages/compiler/src/report-protocol.sigil import { SigilCompilationReportProtocol }

component SigilCompilationHistoryStore {
  goal {
    Supply compiler consumers with optional prior-report evidence for diagnostic
    lifecycle comparison without mutating the selected workspace or making local
    history project authority.
  }

  interface {
    CompilationHistoryStore {
      loadLatest(workspaceIdentity, targetIdentity, reportVersion,
      profileFingerprint) returns the latest compatible CompilationReport from the
      operating-system user cache or returns no prior evidence when history is
      disabled, missing, corrupt, or incompatible

      replaceLatest(CompilationReport) atomically replaces the matching cached report
      unless history is disabled

      replacement failure preserves prior history, reports a non-authoritative host
      warning, and does not change successful compilation settlement
    }
  }
}

expand SigilCompilationHistoryStore {
  logic {
    CompilationHistoryStore {
      Resolve the latest compatible report for the same workspace, target, report
      version, and effective profile from the host-provided operating-system user
      cache.

      Supply that report to SigilCompilationReportProtocol for lifecycle comparison.

      Atomically replace the matching latest compatible report when the caller
      requests replacement and history is enabled. Do not determine when compilation
      cancellation, export, or terminal settlement permits that request.

      On write, sync, or atomic-replacement failure, preserve the preceding cache,
      report a host warning outside CompilationEvent output, and let compilation
      continue toward completed settlement.

      Treat missing, corrupt, or incompatible history as unavailable evidence rather
      than a compilation failure.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    CompilationHistoryStore {
      Store no implicit history inside the selected workspace.

      History lookup and latest-report replacement are enabled by default unless the
      invoking compiler options explicitly disable both.

      Retain only complete CompilationReport values and never treat cached history as
      human approval or durable project authority.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    ExternalCompilationHistory {
      Decision: Keep implicit interactive history outside the repository and make
      durable report transfer explicit.

      Scope: Governs local cache, CI, and team handoff; excludes explicit user-
      selected export destinations.

      Consequences: Compilation remains read-only while lifecycle comparison remains
      available.
    }

    LatestCompatibleReportHistory {
      Decision: Retain only the latest compatible report for each workspace, target,
      report version, and effective profile in the host-provided operating-system
      user cache.

      Scope: Governs implicit local lifecycle comparison; excludes repository files,
      explicit report exports, CI retention, and team handoff.

      Trade-offs: Local history does not preserve a complete timeline and remains
      host-specific.

      Design issues addressed: Diagnostic lifecycle cannot be derived when every run
      is treated as unrelated.

      Discarded alternatives: Repository-local caches and unbounded implicit history
      were rejected because they mutate selected workspaces or create unmanaged
      retention.

      Consequences: Completed runs can derive lifecycle state without making local
      history durable project authority. Cache-write failure remains an observable
      host warning rather than an authoritative compilation failure.
    }

    DefaultCompilationHistory {
      Decision: Enable latest-compatible operating-system user-cache history by
      default and provide one option that disables both lookup and replacement.

      Scope: Governs implicit one-shot compilation history defaults; excludes
      explicit exports, session proposal history, CI retention, and project
      authority.

      Assumptions: Diagnostic lifecycle is more useful when ordinary repeated runs
      can compare with the immediately preceding compatible result.

      Trade-offs: Default retention stores one report per compatible key in private
      host-local cache, while privacy-sensitive callers must opt out explicitly.

      Discarded alternatives: Opt-in history and session-only history were rejected
      because ordinary CLI runs would lose lifecycle continuity or require an
      unrelated proposal session.

      Consequences: Default runs show lifecycle changes without repository mutation;
      disableHistory performs no read or replacement.

      Revisit when: Privacy policy, retention regulation, or deployment constraints
      require opt-in or shorter-lived history.
    }
  }

  cases {
    CompilationHistoryStore {
      Recompiling after resolving one stable finding supplies its prior report so
      SigilCompilationReportProtocol can mark the finding resolved.

      Disabling history reads no prior report and writes no replacement report.

      Corrupt or incompatible history supplies no prior evidence and does not prevent
      completion.

      Replacement failure preserves the prior cache and reports a host warning
      without changing its caller's authoritative outcome.
    }
  }
}
